+    /// value is immutable and no hand-written file writes one (`tagValue`'s
+    /// argument, for every field). `out` holds the set; false when it is
+    /// not known. The chain is safe to evaluate (`Pts.safeChain`), so a
+    /// test it decides may go with it. An empty set is a read that never
+    /// runs with an object: fact 3's ⊥ at the fixpoint.
+    fn fieldValues(s: *Spec, m: *Mod, node: Index, out: *std.ArrayList(u32)) Allocator.Error!bool {
+        if (!s.pts.ok) return false;
+        const ir = m.ir;
+        const field = switch (ir.tag(node)) {
+            .member => node,
+            .ident => try s.localInit(m, @fromBackingInt(@intCast(ir.data(node).lhs))) orelse return false,
